1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,900
Hi, I'm John Webke and I'm a Scoutmaster with 2.358 in Signsville, Indiana.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:08,900
This edition of the Scoutmaster podcast is sponsored by backers like me.

3
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:11,100
And now to you, Scoutmaster.

4
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:26,500
A fire in San Francisco was growing so fast that it had taken over a city block and the whole city was at risk.

5
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,000
Many of the city's fire units responded, but the fire was so intense

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,200
none of them could really get close enough to pour water on the fire.

7
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:41,300
The situation seemed hopeless until one fire engine appeared and sped down the hill past. the other units

8
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:47,100
screeched to a stop close enough to get out their equipment and spray water on the fire,

9
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:51,300
And all of the other firefighters were inspired by the courage of that crew

10
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:54,700
and they joined them to help put the fire out.

11
00:00:54,700 --> 00:01:01,700
And later the mayor presented a commentation of bravery to the fire crew that had sped down the hill

12
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:05,600
and he asked what else the city could do to show their thanks.

13
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:14,000
and the station chief told him that they could really use a new set of brakes on their fire engine.

14
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:23,400
You know good leaders, they respond as expected, but great leaders are prepared for the unexpected.

15
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:26,300
Thanks to Barry Runnels for that story. Thank you, Barry.

16
